From: fan-curve tuning for a 4-node DGX Spark cluster
Subject: [PATCH] userspace: lower the additive request below 62 C and remove the
 0 C / state 0 gap from the performance curve

Applied on top of christopherowen/dgx-spark-fan-control @ userspace/dgx_fan_control.py
(GPL-2.0). The only change is PERFORMANCE_CURVE; everything else is upstream.

Apply from the upstream checkout:
  patch -p1 < 0001-performance-curve.patch
  sudo install -m 755 userspace/dgx_fan_control.py /usr/local/sbin/dgx-fan-control
  sudo systemctl restart dgx-fan-daemon.service

--- a/userspace/dgx_fan_control.py
+++ b/userspace/dgx_fan_control.py
@@ -31,11 +31,15 @@
 # second step. Firmware still takes the maximum of its own demand and this
 # additive request.
 PERFORMANCE_CURVE = (
-    (50.0, 3),   # 4,500 common RPM floor
-    (55.0, 5),   # 6,300
-    (60.0, 8),   # 9,000
-    (65.0, 10),  # 11,250 (fan 0 saturates at 9,000)
-    (70.0, 12),  # 13,500 (both fans at their maxima)
+    (0.0, 1),    # 2,700 always-on floor (never state 0: 0 RPM trap)
+    (52.0, 2),   # 3,600
+    (57.0, 3),   # 4,500
+    (62.0, 4),   # 5,400
+    (66.0, 5),   # 6,300
+    (70.0, 6),   # 7,200
+    (73.0, 8),   # 9,000
+    (76.0, 10),  # 11,250 (fan 0 saturates at 9,000)
+    (78.0, 12),  # 13,500 (both fans at their maxima)
 )
 
 LOG = logging.getLogger("dgx-fan-control")
